## `export_refute_unfold`

``` hol4
Refute.export_refute_unfold : string -> unit
```

Exports the named theorem to the persistent Refute unfolding set,
whose clauses the model finder unfolds during preprocessing.

Every conjunct must have a constant head `c` in its conclusion
(`c t1 ... tn = u`, `c t1 ... tn`, or `~(c t1 ... tn)`): the model
finder looks the clause up by that head.  A clause with no constant
head is dropped with a warning when the model finder builds its tables,
not at export.
